  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU4 Public Order</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The action intends to &lt;strong&gt;support and assist&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;the General Inspectorate of Carabinieri (GIC) &lt;/strong&gt;of the Republic of Moldova, as well as the &lt;strong&gt;Ministry of Internal Affairs (MIA) for its duties related to public order and public security &lt;/strong&gt;activities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For the purposes of the Action the concept of public order is understood as the set of police activities for the prevention and suppression of crimes, which are articulated in two main perspectives:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Crime prevention, with territorial control activities that also ensure the safety of citizens in the event of authorized demonstrations, information gathering, and coordination among law enforcement forces to guarantee &quot;Community Policing&quot; that reflects the European standards of LEAs;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Crime suppression, through investigative activities that target both common and organized criminal phenomena, as well as crowd control and management during unauthorized and violent street demonstrations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The concept of public order is therefore transversely intended, including crime prevention and suppression, and always implies respect for human rights, gender balance, and privacy.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
